{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Renewal is cumulative feedback from current specification through real-world use, gap analysis, and intake-selected re-entry or further observation. Requirements and design evolve, realization is repeatedly derived against current constitutional meaning, and implementation, testing, replay, and scenario gaps feed repricing.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 2955,
          "quote": "Current spec → real-world use case → gap analysis → intake-selected re-entry or observation",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FRenewal%20Path",
          "start_line": 2955
        }
      ],
      "key": "renewal_path",
      "label": "Renewal Path"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Constitutional trace closure closes the constitution over realized behavior and is stricter than documentation completeness. This methodology member selects trace metadata, live-surface supersession and withdrawal, lifecycle/category axes, and bootstrap roles while retaining Design's structure choices and Product's meaning choices.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 2995,
          "quote": "This member separately chooses trace metadata,\nlive-surface supersession/withdrawal, lifecycle/category axes and bootstrap\nroles. Design and Product authorities retain their respective structure and\nmeaning choices; the labels and default scaffold do not determine a verdict.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FTrace%20Closure%20And%20Anti-Drift%20Rule",
          "start_line": 2992
        },
        {
          "end_line": 3049,
          "quote": "Trace closure is stricter than documentation completeness. It is the rule that\ncloses the constitution over realized behavior.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FTrace%20Closure%20And%20Anti-Drift%20Rule%2FDrift%20Signals",
          "start_line": 3048
        }
      ],
      "key": "constitutional_trace_closure",
      "label": "Constitutional trace closure"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Goals orient the current bounded work wave.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3201,
          "quote": "Goals** orient the current bounded work wave.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3201
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_goals",
      "label": "Goals"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Intent states why the system exists and which directional changes are inside or outside scope.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3202,
          "quote": "Intent** states why the system exists and what directional change is in or out of scope.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3202
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_intent",
      "label": "Intent"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Product is the current concrete product-definition surface bridging Intent to Requirements.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3203,
          "quote": "Product** states the current concrete product definition and bridges intent to requirements.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3203
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_product",
      "label": "Product specification surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Requirements state stable obligations that must be true, with explicit acceptance criteria and enough meaning to derive downstream design.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3204,
          "quote": "Requirements** state stable obligations that must be true. They shall carry explicit acceptance criteria and remain sufficient for downstream design derivation",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3204
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_requirements",
      "label": "Requirements"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Design states how requirement truth is realized, downstream of requirements; its choices can include structure, interfaces, carriers, packaging, and tenant boundaries.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3205,
          "quote": "- **Design** states how requirement truth is realized. It is downstream of requirements and may choose structure, interfaces, carriers, packaging, and tenant boundaries.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3205
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_design",
      "label": "Design"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Realization is construction under selected design and execution bindings; code is its software case. Declared evidence sources support observation against requirements, with events, projection, and delta used where selected and adequate direct observation remaining available.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3411,
          "quote": "10. Construct the **Realization** under its selected design and execution\n    binding, and reconcile design, realized behavior and applicable proof\n    before promotion or closure. Code is the software case of this step.\n11. Observe the realized state through its declared evidence sources and compare\n    it with the requirements. Events, projection and delta are used where that\n    binding selects them; adequate direct observation remains available.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FMethod",
          "start_line": 3406
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_realization",
      "label": "Realization"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An ADR is durable design memory organized by the decision boundary that makes acceptance criteria true, rather than by requirement file. Each ADR file remains constitutional source; an accompanying registry is a potentially drifting read model.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3206,
          "quote": "- **ADRs** are durable design memory. They are not a second requirement surface.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FSpecification%20Surface%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3206
        },
        {
          "end_line": 3473,
          "quote": "Write ADRs per decision boundary, not per requirement file.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FADR%20Conventions",
          "start_line": 3473
        },
        {
          "end_line": 3502,
          "quote": "The constitutional source remains each ADR file; a registry is a read model that may drift unless tooling maintains it.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FADR%20Conventions%2FADR%20Folder%20Convention",
          "start_line": 3502
        }
      ],
      "key": "architecture_decision_record",
      "label": "ADR"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A published live domain surface is versioned constitutional history. A project may accumulate multiple such surfaces. Engine code, design documents, tests, and tooling can instead remain mutable implementation surfaces; the artifact's live constitutional status determines the distinction.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3058,
          "quote": "The project may accumulate multiple live domain surfaces over time. A live surface is versioned constitutional history, not scratch space.\n\n- Engine code, design documents, tests, and tooling may be refactored aggressively while they remain mutable implementation surfaces.\n- Live domain artifacts, once published as live constitutional surfaces, are immutable in place.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FLive%20Surface%20Immutability",
          "start_line": 3055
        }
      ],
      "key": "live_domain_surface",
      "label": "Live domain surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "A project intentionally abandons a prior constitutional shape and re-derives itself on a new branch, version line, or methodology basis."
      ],
      "definition": "Fundamental migration is a constitutional reset and controlled adoption. Prior constitutional documents become migration source material. Implementation classifications are carry_across, meaning materially unchanged and explicitly re-adopted; redundant, meaning no longer needed; and rewrite, meaning needed but rebuilt under new requirements and design. Inherited constitutional material is classified as adopted, superseded, deferred, or orphaned.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3072,
          "quote": "A fundamental migration is a constitutional reset, not an in-place refactor.\n\nThis rule applies when a project intentionally abandons a prior constitutional shape and re-derives itself on a new branch, version line, or methodology basis.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FFundamental%20Migration%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3070
        }
      ],
      "key": "fundamental_migration",
      "label": "Fundamental migration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Refactor and migration should be understood as a transformation wave over mutable implementation surfaces, with an in-flight break boundary, a declared affected scope, and a landing state. Explicit compatibility is a current Product feature rather than residual transition plumbing.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3125,
          "quote": "Refactor and migration should be understood as a transformation wave over\nmutable implementation surfaces.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FTransformation%20Wave%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3124
        }
      ],
      "key": "transformation_wave",
      "label": "Transformation wave"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Legacy requirement classifications: Deferred retains an explicit live obligation that is not yet operative or realized; Superseded moves ownership to a newer constitutional surface or design decision; Active remains current live constitutional law; Orphaned is no longer part of the intended system.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3170,
          "quote": "| **Deferred** | Retained in the live surface as an explicit not-yet-operative or not-yet-realized obligation | Keep with an honest deferment surface and do not present as current closure |\n| **Superseded** | Ownership has moved to a newer constitutional surface or design decision | Add Implements/Supersedes to the governing design record |\n| **Active** | Remains live constitutional law in the current surface | Must have an owning design decision — write or update one |\n| **Orphaned** | No longer part of the intended system | Remove or explicitly supersede |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FLegacy%20Classification%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3167
        }
      ],
      "key": "legacy_requirement_classification",
      "label": "Legacy requirement classification"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The independent requirement axes are lifecycle status—Active, Deferred, Superseded, Orphaned—and requirement category—Capability, Constraint / Guarantee, Governance, Verification. Status answers constitutional membership and operative/deferred state; Category answers the kind of project truth asserted.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3191,
          "quote": "These axes answer different questions. Lifecycle status says whether the requirement still belongs in the constitution and whether it is operative or explicitly deferred. Requirement category says what kind of project truth it asserts. A live requirement is incomplete if either axis is missing.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FRequirement%20Classification%20Rules",
          "start_line": 3191
        }
      ],
      "key": "requirement_classification_axes",
      "label": "Requirement classification axes"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Product Definition template is templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json, copied as stdo_default.json for a singleton default or stdo_<label>.json for a named definition. URI bindings select actual carriers. Defaults bind constitution.stdo.basis to a shared versioned installed STDO store; specification/GOALS.md, INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, and requirements/ to constitutional surfaces; build_tenants/ to common and tenant-local realization; and .ai-workspace/ to sprints, tickets, and comments. The illustrated topology includes build_tenants/common and default, plus ticket backlog, active, and completed lanes.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3232,
          "quote": "Every STDO-defined product begins from\n`templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json`. Copy it to the product's\ndefinition root as `stdo_default.json` for a singleton default project or as\n`stdo_<label>.json` for a named product definition. An existing project fills\nthe URI bindings over its current layout; adoption does not require moving,\nrenaming, or duplicating existing authority or realization surfaces.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FBootstrap%20Rule",
          "start_line": 3227
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_definition_bootstrap",
      "label": "Product Definition bootstrap"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Method is the source-described ordered intake, feature-change, bootstrap/repricing, and real-use-gap procedure. Its substantive intake begins with classification, lawful constitutional re-entry, and identification of the affected downstream span.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3383,
          "quote": "1. Triage the intake and classify the change.\n2. Determine the lawful re-entry point into the constitutional chain.\n3. Identify the affected downstream span that must remain consistent.\n4. Only then treat the work as implementation, repricing, or release-bound change.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#Spec-Driven%20Homeostatic%20Methodology%2FMethod",
          "start_line": 3380
        }
      ],
      "key": "spec_method",
      "label": "Method"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "STDO Reference Frame Baseline is an optional specialized role and evaluation profile mapping existing law to engagement, specialist, and testing frames. Its headings' word Derived means application plus optional profile choices, not a uniquely compelled inventory. It independently owns neither execution protocol nor Product bindings.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1,
          "quote": "# STDO Reference Frame Baseline",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline",
          "start_line": 1
        },
        {
          "end_line": 94,
          "quote": "This document is an optional specialized role and evaluation profile. “Derived”\nin its frame headings means an application of shared law with the additional\nprofile choices identified below, not a uniquely forced role inventory. It has no\nindependent ownership of STDO's execution protocol or of any Product binding.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FStatus%20And%20Authority%20Boundary",
          "start_line": 91
        }
      ],
      "key": "reference_frame_baseline",
      "label": "STDO Reference Frame Baseline"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An engagement frame is a Reference Frame Method frame evaluating selection, construction, assessment, or disposition of governed work. This profile's engagement frames are Executive, Worker, and Reviewer.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 234,
          "quote": "An **engagement frame** is a `REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md` frame whose evaluation\nfamily concerns selection, construction, assessment, or disposition of governed\nwork. Executive, Worker, and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FEngagement%20frame",
          "start_line": 232
        }
      ],
      "key": "engagement_frame",
      "label": "Engagement frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Needed by one engagement evaluation and activated with declared evaluation, basis, material manifold, authority, evidence, result algebra, and capability envelope."
      ],
      "definition": "A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity, release, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical, or capability frame. Mere existence as a method member, file, component, or lens does not establish frame status.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 242,
          "quote": "A **specialist frame** is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity,\nrelease, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical, or capability\nframe needed by one engagement evaluation. A method member, file, component, or\nlens becomes a frame only when its evaluation, basis, material manifold,\nauthority, evidence, result algebra, and capability envelope are declared.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FSpecialist%20frame",
          "start_line": 238
        }
      ],
      "key": "specialist_frame",
      "label": "Specialist frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation archetype, not a selected carrier, component, actor, architecture, owner, or implementation. Multiple frames may instantiate one family; one frame may cover multiple families only while its evaluation and results preserve every material distinction.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 256,
          "quote": "The family does not select a concrete carrier, component, actor, architecture,\nowner, or implementation. One project may instantiate several frames in one\nfamily. One declared frame may cover several families only when its evaluation\nand result relations preserve every material distinction rather than flattening\nthem behind one broad label.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FGeneric%20specialist-frame%20family",
          "start_line": 252
        }
      ],
      "key": "generic_specialist_family",
      "label": "Generic specialist-frame family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A testing frame is a specialist evaluation that executes or observes a declared subject to discriminate an exact claim through an explicit oracle, evidence population, path boundary, and falsification condition. A test file, suite, runner, fixture, scenario label, coverage percentage, or actor alone is not a testing frame.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 264,
          "quote": "A **testing frame** is a specialist frame whose evaluation executes or observes\na declared subject to discriminate one exact claim through an explicit oracle,\nevidence population, path boundary, and falsification condition. A test file,\nsuite, runner, fixture, scenario label, coverage percentage, or actor does not\nbecome a testing frame merely by existing.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FTesting%20frame",
          "start_line": 260
        }
      ],
      "key": "testing_frame",
      "label": "Testing frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The authoritative Product path is the declared ordinary causal composition from supported user or Public entry through exact selected interfaces, owners, state transitions, effects, persistence, recovery, and required outcome projection.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 275,
          "quote": "An **authoritative Product path** is the declared ordinary causal composition\nfrom a supported user or Public entry through the exact selected interfaces,\nowners, state transitions, effects, persistence and recovery boundaries, and\noutcome projection required by the Product claim.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FAuthoritative%20Product%20path",
          "start_line": 272
        }
      ],
      "key": "authoritative_product_path",
      "label": "Authoritative Product path"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Material combinatorial complexity is the claim-relative population of independent dimensions and interactions whose combinations can change an outcome, violate an invariant, select another authority path, or expose failure. Unit dimensions include module-owned public contracts, algebraic operators, calculation regimes, states, transitions, boundary classes, and failures. Cross-participant interface, Product, persistence, configuration, and user-role combinations belong at integration, end-to-end, or user-acceptance boundaries.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 290,
          "quote": "**Material combinatorial complexity** is the claim-relative population of\nindependent dimensions and interactions whose combinations can change an\noutcome, violate an invariant, select another authority path, or expose a\nfailure. At unit altitude it includes module-owned laws, including behavior at\nthe public module contract, and their algebraic operators, calculation regimes,\nstates, transitions, boundary classes, and failure cases. Cross-participant\ninterface, Product, persistence, configuration, and user-role combinations\nbelong to integration, end-to-end, or user-acceptance frames rather than being\nmocked away and counted as unit evidence.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FMaterial%20combinatorial%20complexity",
          "start_line": 282
        }
      ],
      "key": "material_combinatorial_complexity",
      "label": "Material combinatorial complexity"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "The coordinated branch is selected under existing project decision authority."
      ],
      "definition": "Executive selects or confirms bounded activation configuration and consumes closed results. Its bounded delivery view includes the long-term outcome, current MVP/release mandate, obligations, dependencies, and returned results needed for priority, disposition, and next authorized action. The workspace holds the durable frontier; Executive need not load all Product material, history, or Worker context. It may be direct human authority or an admitted bounded proxy, and is not a universal semantic owner, controller, manager service, or runtime observer.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 301,
          "quote": "**Executive** is the profile label for the frame that selects or confirms the\nbounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and Reviewer\nresults under existing project decision authority. It maintains a sufficient\nbounded delivery view of the long-term outcome, current MVP or release mandate,\nunresolved obligations, dependencies and exact returned results needed to\nassign priority, apply disposition and select the next authorised action.\nThe underlying workspace carries the durable frontier; the Executive need not\nload the whole Product, every historical result or every worker's context.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FProfile%20Terms%2FExecutive",
          "start_line": 294
        }
      ],
      "key": "executive_frame",
      "label": "Executive"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Activated with sufficient execution intake and inherited bounded operation authority."
      ],
      "definition": "Worker is the bounded constructor reference frame owning construction and self-review within exact intake. Its evaluation asks whether the authorized outcome can be built through the smallest coherent causal cone, preserving affected governing relations and disposing competing paths. Its manifold includes entities, lifecycles, transformations, authorities, capabilities, algorithms, inputs/outputs, dependencies, seams, failures, and proof obligations. Coordinates identify activation, source checkpoint, workspace, inputs, dependencies, configuration, actor envelope, outputs, candidate, and evidence. Evidence includes implementation, tests and their source, analysis, generated artifacts, claimed installed/operational behavior, reconstruction, mutations, and transition evidence; competence covers method, domain, implementation, tools, access, and finite context.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 493,
          "quote": "**Worker** is the profile label for `STDO-UP-020`'s bounded constructor role\nwhen activated as a reference frame. It owns construction and self-review\ninside its exact intake through the operation authority inherited from the\ngoverning work relation. It does not acquire admission, publication, acceptance,\nor continuation authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FWorker",
          "start_line": 489
        },
        {
          "end_line": 751,
          "quote": "| evaluation family | Can the exact authorized outcome be constructed through the smallest coherent causal cone while preserving every affected governing relation and disposing competing paths? |",
