      ],
      "definition": "Reviewer is independent live-surface evaluation consumed by the assessment relation. It evaluates one exact candidate claim and basis, applicable law, competing authority, proof masking, and composition coverage, returning a closed result and evidence-bound technical triage where findings exist. Its basis includes scope/exclusions, evidence population, severity scale, review carrier, and independence. Its manifold covers producers/consumers, authority seams, competing paths, claimed failure/recovery/installed/reconstruction surfaces, test/fixture semantics, historical counterexamples, and supportable finding implications. Coordinates retain candidate, source and authority revision, configuration, dependency, evidence population, severity scale, installed subject, review time, and Reviewer identity. Evidence is independently acquired live authority, implementation, tests, artifacts, history, operational evidence, mutations, replay/reconstruction, and reproduced observations; competence includes assurance, counterexample search, technical triage, access, context, and independence.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 502,
          "quote": "**Reviewer** is the profile label for the independent live-surface evaluation\nconsumed by the `STDO-UP-020` assessment relation and governed by\n`STDO-UP-007` and `STDO-UP-022` when activated as a reference frame. It\nevaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result with evidence-bound\ntechnical triage when a finding exists. It does not implement the repair,\nassign priority, apply disposition, or activate the next frame.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FReviewer",
          "start_line": 497
        },
        {
          "end_line": 785,
          "quote": "| evaluation family | Is this the exact claimed subject and basis? Does it satisfy the applicable STDO and project relations without competing authority, proof masking, or an unevaluated composition boundary? For each finding, what evidence-bound severity and technical implications follow? |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Reviewer%20Frame",
          "start_line": 785
