    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A Product-chain basis records a single Product or directed chain, distinguishing mutable Source Project, current Product Definition, candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product, and composition-edge roles. Each Development Product role binds an exact underlying Install. Each edge declares source/target roles, authority/contracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal, and invalidation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 471,
          "quote": "A governed outcome may concern one Product or an explicit directed chain of\nProducts. Its basis records the distinct role of every mutable Source Project,\ncurrent Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product,\nInstall, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product, and composition\nedge. Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying Install\nidentity. Each edge names its source and target roles, governing authority and\ncontracts, lifecycle, evidence boundary, refusal, and invalidation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FProduct-Chain%20Basis",
