      "definition": "Technical triage is Reviewer-owned assessment of a finding against its exact claim and basis. Evidence and capability permitting, it records affected claim/failure, Product-scale severity, causal assessment/confidence, blast radius and affected users/paths/relations, workaround/containment, repair complexity/regression risk/dependencies, and uncertainty with needed evidence. Severity grades consequences if manifested. Priority orders responses by full Product outcome, likelihood/exposure, MVP/release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, delay cost, and capacity. Current-boundary effect is Executive's decision that a finding blocks promotion, requires narrowing, or may remain an explicit residual.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 531,
          "quote": "**Severity** grades consequence if the finding manifests. **Priority** orders\nresponse relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood and exposure,\ncurrent MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, cost of delay, and\navailable capacity. Reviewer grades severity. Executive assigns priority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%2C%20and%20boundary%20effect",
