    {
      "conditions": [
        "Successful Worker activation has occurred."
      ],
      "definition": "A work result is closed Worker output to its declared consumer, Executive in the coordinated branch. Its finer domain variants—candidate_ready, refused, incomplete, re_entry_requested—are neither a separate result algebra nor semantic dispositions. It carries the shared core record, actual performance/effects, and the predicate that requested candidate and transition evidence are available on the activated basis within admitted grant bounds. Delivery time is part of that predicate only where required by the grant.",
      "exceptions": [
        "activation_refusal returns to the assigning authority or declared carrier without creating a Worker activation or work result."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 571,
          "quote": "The work-result variants are finer domain outcomes, not another result algebra\nor STDO semantic dispositions. Every result carries the shared core record,\nthe actual performance and effect state, and one exact predicate: “the requested\ncandidate and transition evidence are available on the activated basis within\nthe admitted grant's declared bounds”. The bounds include a delivery time only\nwhere the grant requires it. A later delivery does not repair a missed bound\non the original predicate; changed bounds identify a successor claim.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FWork%20result",
