    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An exact candidate is the subject identity required for STDO-UP-020 transition evidence and STDO-UP-007 review traceability. Applicable STDO-UP-022 generic-method qualification freezes the construction result before material reference exposure; otherwise an immutable identity or equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the assessment stabilizes review. This profile creates no constitutional lifecycle state named frozen.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 617,
          "quote": "An **exact candidate** is the subject identity required by `STDO-UP-020`\ntransition evidence and `STDO-UP-007` review traceability. Where\n`STDO-UP-022` generic method qualification applies, its construction result is\nfrozen before material reference exposure as that clause requires. Elsewhere,\nthis profile stabilizes the review subject through an immutable identity or an\nequivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claimed assessment.\n\nThis profile does not create a new constitutional lifecycle state named\n`frozen`.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FExact%20candidate",
