    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Baseline-adoption projection applies faithful projection from the Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis into this engagement, preserving selected mapping, outcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates, and revision conditions. Adoption remains the source owner's decision.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 627,
          "quote": "A **baseline-adoption projection** applies\n[Faithful projection](TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.md#faithful-projection) from the\nProduct-owned [Project Reference-Frame Basis](SPEC_METHOD.md#collective-reference-frame-basis)\nto this profile's engagement. Its material distinctions are the selected mapping,\noutcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions in\n[Adopt This Baseline](#adopt-this-baseline). Adoption remains that source\nowner's decision.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action%2FBaseline-adoption%20projection",
          "start_line": 621
        }
      ],
      "key": "baseline_adoption_projection",
      "label": "Baseline-adoption projection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Active configuration distinguishes authority precedence, temporal/evidence flow, and frame topology. Precedence determines existing work-selection, admission, disposition, and re-entry authority; flow carries activation packets and closed results; topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation, or composition. Evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence are separate activation relations. Engagement frame plus material specialists, exact subject/basis, and capable actor denotes one activation, without requiring a Cartesian-product schema or universal runtime.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 653,
          "quote": "The active configuration uses three distinct relation structures:\n\n1. **authority precedence** determines which existing surface may select work,\n   admit a frame configuration, dispose a result, or require re-entry;\n2. **temporal and evidence flow** carries activation packets and closed results;\n   and\n3. **frame topology** records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation,\n   or composition among the evaluations actually used, while evaluation and\n   Reviewer-assurance independence remain separate activation relations.\n\nThese structures may align in one case. They are not one hierarchy.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FNon-Hierarchical%20Frame%20Configuration",
          "start_line": 643
        }
      ],
      "key": "non_hierarchical_configuration",
      "label": "Non-hierarchical frame configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A steel thread is the smallest real runnable path from supported Product entry through selected composition to a material outcome. Executive sequences early establishment, bounded expansion, or extension/revalidation of an existing thread by consequential uncertainty, dependency/interface reach, and failure impact.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 718,
          "quote": "Executive sequences delivery around a steel thread: the smallest real,\nrunnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through\nthe selected composition. Establish that path early and expand it in bounded\nincrements. Where it already exists, extend or revalidate the affected\nthread. Select increments by consequential uncertainty, dependency and\ninterface reach, and failure impact.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Executive%20Frame%2FSteel-Thread%20Delivery",
          "start_line": 713
