    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["generic_specialist_inventory", "generic_specialist_family"],
      "conditions": ["The generic set is adopted and a family instance is activated."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 846,
          "quote": "This profile declares the following generic frame families for Product work.\nEach row is an evaluation archetype under `REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md`, not a\ncomplete frame declaration. An adopting project binds the exact subject,\nbasis, material manifold, coordinates, invariants, authority, evidence,\nexclusions, result algebra, capability envelope, dependencies, and\ninvalidation conditions for every activated instance.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Generic%20Specialist%20Frame%20Set",
          "start_line": 841
        }
      ],
      "key": "specialist_owner_and_falsifier_boundaries",
      "statement": "Every activated instance binds exact subject/basis/manifold/coordinates/invariants/authority/evidence/exclusions/result algebra/capability/dependencies/invalidators. Twelve archetypes do not require twelve actors/components. Their existing owners retain decisions and outputs remain bounded evaluations/evidence: Product and requirements own meaning/acceptance; composition's named authorities/contracts own edges while each Product retains meaning; accepted Design under Product/requirements owns structure; component design owns only its bounded decision with parent/sibling/runtime owners retained; Product/interface/identity/security/design own Public Boundary; Product/domain/identity/requirements/design own Entity; Product/requirements/accepted Ontology/design/named operation owner own Operator; existing named authorities own Owner relations; applicable Product/requirement/design/artifact/runtime/admission owners own Effect; UP-023 and tradeoff owner select foundations; Product/identity/release/dependency/packaging/design own Install; claim owners own meaning and testing/assurance/review/Product/release own Proof evaluation/acceptance. Immediate falsifiers respectively include downstream/predecessent/local rewriting or subject substitution; inferred composition/identity or one Product redefining another; implementation resolving open design or undeclared material/competing structure; omitted far-side seam or absorbed parent/sibling decision; Public interpreting owner meaning/hidden sequencing/exposing interior truth/unsupported paths; wrappers/files/caches/processes replacing identity or collapsed lifecycle; executable labels mistaken for semantic atoms, hidden operators, or generic mechanics recast as domain law; recreated judgments/authorship transfer/widened proxy grants; collapsed effects, owner-bypassing mutation, compensation as semantic rollback, or rival writable read; unexamined incumbent preference, reproduced richer lawful foundations, favorable unknown scores, or reuse authority transfer; ambient/source/registry/fixture/rebuild/moving-workspace substitution for Install; and proof of wrong claim/path, recreated owner meaning, aggregate-green substitution, or undetectable subject mutation.",
      "uncertainty": "Named domain owners supply predicates beyond these archetype descriptions."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["generic_specialist_inventory", "generic_specialist_family"],
      "conditions": ["An outcome is governed under the adopted generic inventory."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 898,
          "quote": "These are inventory treatments, not alternate evaluation verdicts. When\nevaluating “every family is accounted for on this outcome and basis”, supported\nmaterial instantiation, supported non-materiality or an explicit justified\nresidual satisfies that family's accounting predicate. An established omission\nor disproved treatment defeats it (`falsified`); undecided treatment or missing\nreason is `indeterminate`; an unusable basis is `invalid_basis`; evaluation\nscope/capability outside the frame is `out_of_frame`. Apply core conjunction to\nthe required family-accounting predicates and retain performance and effects.\nAccounting for a residual does not establish adequate coverage or the family's\nunderlying Product claim. Those claims use\n[Operational Full Coverage](REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#operational-full-coverage)\nand each family's exact evaluation predicate, respectively.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Generic%20Specialist%20Frame%20Set",
          "start_line": 887
        }
      ],
      "key": "specialist_inventory_and_coverage",
      "statement": "Every family is recorded as materially instantiated by exact frames/authoritative acquisition, capable-authority-evidenced non-material, or explicit uncovered/conditional/conflicted/scope-capability residual; any actual out_of_frame result is separately referenced. For the accounting predicate, supported instantiation/non-materiality/justified residual→satisfied; established omission/disproved treatment→falsified; undecided/missing reason→indeterminate; unusable basis→invalid_basis; outside evaluation scope/capability→out_of_frame. Conjoin required accounting predicates and retain performance/effects. Accounted residual is neither sufficient coverage nor underlying claim truth. Missing named actors/files/components/runtime objects do not prove non-materiality. Families overlap without topology-created precedence or authority transfer; explicit relations cross material context seams. Refinement only opens for parent-material distinctions; children record parent contract, purpose, entities, identities/lifecycles, semantic owners, direct sibling seams, invariants, and forbidden competitors. Coverage unions admissible observations; composite claims conjoin required predicates and material seams, using declared cross-frame relations without a dominant family. Consumer-specific frames/topologies remain outside this baseline and require their own authority.",
      "uncertainty": "Operational Full Coverage and result-conjunction definitions are outside the supplied source."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["testing_frame", "user_acceptance_frame", "end_to_end_frame", "integration_frame", "unit_test_frame"],
      "conditions": ["The profile supports Product promotion, closure, or release assurance."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 968,
          "quote": "These frames may overlap and one execution may supply evidence to several of\nthem. Every result remains bound to its own claim. A label such as `UAT`, `E2E`,\n`integration`, or `unit` has no assurance value without the corresponding frame\ndeclaration.\n\nApply [Construction assurance](FOUNDATIONS.md#construction-assurance) to each\nselected testing claim. The frame binds its requirement or refinement source,\nasserted predicate, observation basis and required assurance through the\napplication below. These bindings add no test archetype or mandatory actor;\nthis profile's adoption, ordinary-path and exact-subject conditions still apply.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set",
          "start_line": 959
        }
      ],
      "key": "testing_frame_configuration",
      "statement": "Configure testing by exact claim/subject/path/population/oracle/falsification boundary, never runner kind. Evidence supports only what is evaluated. Four archetypes are profile choices, not consequences of foundational axioms alone; Spec assurance/testing owners, Product, and accepted Design select actual claims, required populations, and acceptance. UAT covers supported-user outcome, E2E the complete runnable causal path, integration material composition interactions, and unit module-owned law. Internal unit complexity controls proportional strategy/size, not eligibility. One execution may evidence several frames but every result retains its own coordinates/claim; labels alone confer no assurance. Where generic specialists are adopted, testing provides claim-congruent Proof evidence without a testing hierarchy or aggregate-green authority. Bind each selected claim's requirement/refinement source, predicate, observation basis, and required construction assurance while retaining adoption, ordinary-path, and exact-subject conditions.",
      "uncertainty": "Construction assurance and the detailed Spec testing owners are referenced, not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["user_acceptance_frame"],
      "conditions": ["A user-outcome claim is evaluated."],
      "exceptions": [
        "Admitted harnessed sandbox UAT may substitute declared external worker/transport only within the composed relations actually exercised.",
        "Automation is allowed only if it faithfully occupies the user's admitted capabilities and path."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 998,
          "quote": "User acceptance is the primary Product-outcome evidence frame when the claim is\nthat a user can use the Product. It may be automated only when automation\nfaithfully occupies the declared user frame and does not gain a path or\ncapability unavailable to that user. Automation can execute acceptance\nevidence; it cannot assume acceptance authority.\n\nWhere `SPEC_METHOD.md` admits harnessed sandbox UAT, a deterministic, fake,\nrecorded, or injected external worker or transport limits the result to the\ncomposed Product relations actually exercised. It does not prove that the live\nexternal boundary works. When a Product or release claim depends on real\nexternal compute or transport, live sandbox UAT is mandatory for that claim;\nunit, integration, semantic, end-to-end evidence that uses the substitute, and\nharnessed UAT green are not sufficient.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set%2FDerived%20User-Acceptance%20Frame",
          "start_line": 986
        }
      ],
      "key": "user_acceptance_evidence_limits",
      "statement": "UAT is primary evidence for user usability claims but grants bounded evaluation only, not Product meaning or acceptance authority, including to automated actors. Apply Product/requirement outcomes, supported-interface/identity/UX/safety/persistence/release law, RF-001..017 and UP-001/008/022. Exclude source imports, private APIs, injected Product state, test-only endpoints, hidden admin capability, undeclared fixtures/substitutes, doubles at claimed live boundaries, compatibility bypass, and internal success substituted for user outcome. Substituted evidence cannot prove the live external boundary; real external compute/transport claims require live sandbox UAT and cannot be closed by substitute-based unit/integration/semantic/E2E/harnessed green. Material Product/interface/user role/capability/configuration/dependency/substitution mode/data contract/runnable subject/acceptance/ordinary-path changes invalidate affected reliance.",
      "uncertainty": "The admission conditions for harnessed sandbox UAT and the cited invariants are external."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["end_to_end_frame"],
      "conditions": ["An exact end-to-end Product claim is evaluated."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1019,
          "quote": "The expected output is necessary but not sufficient. Reaching it through a\nforbidden or obsolete path falsifies the end-to-end claim. A test is not end to\nend merely because it starts and finishes in one process, crosses many lines,\nor carries an end-to-end label.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set%2FDerived%20End-To-End%20Frame",
          "start_line": 1016
        }
      ],
      "key": "end_to_end_evidence_limits",
      "statement": "Apply Product/design composition, exact-subject/assurance congruence, required path singularity, lifecycle, authority, persistence, replay, recovery, and release law. Bounded observation may expose internal evidence but cannot bypass, repair, replace, or reinterpret the Product path. Exclude source-only substitutes for runnable claims, entry bypass, doubles at real boundaries, test-only routing, hidden retry/repair, omitted persistence or fresh-process boundaries, and output equality without path evidence. Expected output is necessary but insufficient; forbidden/obsolete paths falsify the claim. Process span, lines crossed, or labels do not establish E2E status. Material artifact/Install/dependency/configuration/interface/owner/path/lifecycle/persistence/recovery/projection/test semantics/evidence population changes invalidate affected reliance.",
