      "conditions": ["A declared composition-boundary claim is evaluated."],
      "exceptions": ["A substitute can support a deliberately narrower claim only with explicit equivalence boundary and exclusions."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1040,
          "quote": "A substitute or test double may support a deliberately narrower claim only when\nits equivalence boundary and exclusions are explicit. Its result cannot be\npromoted to evidence that the real participant or Product composition was\nexercised.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set%2FDerived%20Integration%20Frame",
          "start_line": 1037
        }
      ],
      "key": "integration_evidence_limits",
      "statement": "Apply declared interface/composition law, complete participant admission, applicable atomicity/reconstruction, and UP-022 assurance boundary. Integration authority is bounded to its boundary: it cannot establish unevaluated Product outcomes or authorize substitute participants. Exclude mocks/stubs hiding real contracts, one-sided assertions, happy-path-only exchange, helper-call equivalence, flattened versions/states, or unguided projection to the whole Product. Narrow substitute evidence cannot be promoted to proof of real participant or Product composition. Material participant/interface/carrier/state/configuration/dependency/timing/failure/recovery/interaction-population changes invalidate affected reliance.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["unit_test_frame", "material_combinatorial_complexity"],
      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1083,
          "quote": "This profile does not waive the module-derived unit lane. It binds that lane to\nmodule-owned law and the smallest congruent evidence population. Low internal\ncombinatorial complexity justifies a small lane, not omission and not hundreds\nof implementation-shaped tests. Unit-test volume has no independent closure\nvalue.\n\nNo Product, user-outcome, installed-path, cross-module composition, or release\nclaim may be closed from unit evidence, regardless of test count, assertion\ncount, source coverage, mutation score, runtime, or historical pass rate.\nTreating unit green as broader assurance is a frame error.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set%2FDerived%20Unit-Test%20Frame",
          "start_line": 1074
        }
      ],
      "key": "unit_evidence_limits",
      "statement": "Every coded module requires the Design Method's module-derived unit lane, including public module contracts; use the smallest congruent population and complexity-proportional strategy. Apply module ownership/unit-proof and material Ontology/IACS/domain/sequence/state/algorithm/error relations. Unit results retain exact law/population, counterexamples, residual combinations, and invalidators, and provide local evidence only—no Product/installed/integration/UAT/architecture/path-selection/release authority. Exclude broader outcomes, composition, supported-user paths, installation/packaging, real external participants, orchestration, mocked-away interfaces, incidental branches/private helper layout, and count/coverage as broader assurance. Implementation-repeating or incidental-branch oracles are weak/circular evidence. Composition/orchestration/configuration/persistence/ownership/user-interaction complexity needs integration/E2E/UAT; mocking does not make it unit evidence. Low complexity permits a small lane, never omission or mass implementation-shaped tests. No broader Product/user/installed/composition/release closure follows from any test/assertion count, coverage, mutation score, runtime, or pass history. Material Ontology/IACS/boundary/law/algorithm/state space/numerical regime/implementation/oracle/generator/population change invalidates affected reliance.",
      "uncertainty": "Module-derived unit law and IACS are referenced but not defined here."
    },
    {
