      "conditions": ["A claim's testing coverage and strategy are selected."],
      "exceptions": [
        "Covering-array reduction is lawful only if omitted higher-order interactions cannot change the claim according to the basis, or remain explicit residuals."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1151,
          "quote": "The activated frame declares the finite interaction population and why its\ncovering set is adequate. Pairwise or other covering-array reduction is lawful\nonly where the basis explains why omitted higher-order interactions cannot\nchange the claim or retains them as residuals. High-consequence authority,\npersistence, concurrency, recovery, migration, and historically failure-prone\nrelations normally require explicit higher-strength combinations.\n\nSource, line, branch, and function coverage may diagnose whether code was\nvisited. They do not establish semantic combination coverage, authoritative\npath selection, user-outcome coverage, or the absence of a rival path.\n\nThe admitted work authority selects the needed testing assurance under\n[Risk and assurance selection](FOUNDATIONS.md#risk-and-assurance-selection).\nBind material failure consequences, coverage, uncertainty and action/acceptance\nconditions when comparing candidate testing strategies. Include acquisition,\nimpact analysis, execution and assessment in the relevant cost boundary;\nretain estimates separately from measurements. A numeric confidence claim\nuses that owner's probability, dependence and calibration conditions, not\nthe testing-value index or test count as a substitute.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#STDO%20Reference%20Frame%20Baseline%2FDerived%20Product%20Testing%20Frame%20Set%2FCombinatorial%20Coverage%20And%20Testing-Value%20Index",
          "start_line": 1133
        }
      ],
      "key": "combinatorial_coverage_requirements",
      "statement": "Declare finite interaction population and covering-set adequacy. Common Product factors include role/capability; operation/composition; definition/owner/implementation/dependency; lifecycle/persisted state; configuration/version; process/continuation/retry/re-entry/recovery; success/refusal/malformed result/partial failure/rival paths; fresh process/replay/reconstruction/migration; and visible outcome/projection. Pairwise reduction has the stated evidence-or-residual condition; high-consequence authority/persistence/concurrency/recovery/migration/historical failures normally need explicit stronger interactions. Touching many interfaces on a sunny path is not combination proof. Counts of tests/assertions/files/lines/branches/mocks/snapshots/runners do not index value; code coverage diagnoses visits but proves neither semantic combinations, authoritative paths, user outcomes, nor absent rivals. Admitted work authority selects assurance; compare strategies with failure consequences, coverage, uncertainty, and action/acceptance conditions, counting acquisition, impact analysis, execution, and assessment costs while separating estimates from measurements. Numeric confidence requires the owning probability/dependence/calibration conditions, not this index or counts.",
      "uncertainty": "The risk/assurance selection owner's probability and calibration conditions are not supplied."
    }
